    "line": 17,
    "body": "`Invoke-MathToolCli` treats each pipeline output object from `pwsh` as a “line” (`Lines = @($standardOutput)`), but PowerShell output objects are not the same as stdout lines (e.g., a single string containing embedded newlines would still count as 1). Since the contract is explicitly “exactly one stdout line”, capture stdout as raw text and split into real lines before asserting counts."
  },
  {
    "id": 3981709382,
    "path": "math-tool.ps1",
    "line": 9,
    "body": "`math-tool.ps1` is intended to be dot-sourced as a library for unit tests, but `Set-StrictMode -Version Latest` and `$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'` execute at top level. When dot-sourced, these mutate the caller’s scope (and can break other scripts/tests that dot-source this file). Prefer limiting these side effects to direct execution, and/or scoping them inside `Get-Fibonacci`."
  }
]

